      ":question/id": "0d423064-4228-5628-8ea8-e3830733329e",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186096700/ee7abbf740e4bb8edbe40a3802001fd637abe14dbbf763d1de07b9940a01f7da.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{c}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{b}$. So, $\\mathbf{c}\\ne -2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $\\mathbf{d}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{d}$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$. So, $\\mathbf{d}=-\\mathbf{e}$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{c}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{b}$. So, $\\mathbf{c}=2\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true.",
